Add ice_comms_triple_vlan-1.3.2.0.pkg, a variant of the ICE COMMS DDP
package that enables transparent passthrough of a third inner VLAN tag
to a SR-IOV Virtual Function.

The standard COMMS DDP package operates in Double VLAN Mode (DVM),
which gives the hardware two VLAN tag slots: one consumed by the outer
port-VLAN (used for DCB traffic classification) and one visible to the
VF. Any third tag present in the frame is stripped before delivery. This
package extends the classification pipeline so that the third tag is
treated as opaque payload and forwarded intact to the VF.

The outermost tag remains subject to DVM constraints because it drives
DCB scheduling; only 0x8100 and 0x88a8 are supported as the outermost
TPID. The middle and innermost tags, including 0x88e7 (ETH_P_8021AH),
are forwarded transparently without modification. Frames with 0x88e7 as
the outermost tag are out of scope as they conflict with DCB
classification.

Testing hints:
  # Install ice_comms_triple_vlan package - refer to Dynamic Device
  # Personalization section in:
  # Documentation/networking/device_drivers/ethernet/intel/ice.rst
  # in kernel tree.
  modprobe ice
  echo 1 > /sys/class/net/$PF/device/sriov_numvfs
  ip link set dev $PF vf 0 trust on spoofchk off
  ip link set $VF promisc on
  ethtool -K $PF rx-vlan-offload off tx-vlan-offload off
  ethtool -K $VF rx-vlan-offload off tx-vlan-offload off
  # Create triple VLAN stack on link partner and ping through VF:
  ip link add link $LP type vlan proto 802.1Q id 100
  ip link add link $LP.100 type vlan proto 802.1ad id 200
  ip link add link $LP.100.200 type vlan proto 802.1Q id 300
  ip addr add 192.168.1.1/24 dev $LP.100.200
  ip link set $LP.100 up; ip link set $LP.100.200 up; ip link set $LP.100.200.300 up
  # On the VF side create matching stack and verify ping succeeds:
  ip link add link $VF type vlan proto 802.1Q id 200
  ip link add link $VF.200 type vlan proto 802.1Q id 300
  ip addr add 192.168.1.2/24 dev $VF.200.300
  ip link set $VF.200 up; ip link set $VF.200.300 up
  ping -c 3 192.168.1.1

